WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.472
For this module, we will intentionally work with a small messy dataset.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:10.547
It contains several realistic problems that you may see in real projects.

00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:19.362
There is a duplicated order, missing values, an invalid date, inconsistent capitalization and spacing,

00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:25.042
a numeric column stored as text, and a few values that look suspicious.

00:00:25.042 --> 00:00:27.858
The goal is not to fix everything immediately.

00:00:28.564 --> 00:00:32.856
Before we change anything, we should understand what is wrong.

00:00:32.856 --> 00:00:36.751
That is an important habit in professional analytics.

00:00:36.751 --> 00:00:44.086
If you start editing values too quickly, you may remove evidence that helps explain how the problem happened.

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:52.256
For example, a value of eleven hundred may be a data-entry error, but it may also be a legitimate large order.

00:00:52.256 --> 00:00:58.361
A missing region may need to stay missing if we do not have enough information to recover it.

00:00:58.361 --> 00:01:06.171
As we work through the module, we will use the same dataset so you can see exactly how each cleaning step changes it.
